 "novel_mechanics_found": "L6 decoded far beyond prior scouting, though not yet won. (1) SHELF-RIDING ESCAPE: the three lower 1-shelves (rows 54-59) form a 6-phase B-cycle whose shapes overlap; the avatar can step DOWN out of the lower-middle room onto a shelf when a phase puts one under cols 18-19, then ride/step between phases (a B-press is refused-with-tick if the next phase would strand the avatar) all the way west to the corridor (cols 6-11) - first time the L6 room system was escaped. (2) The vertical C column (6-control rotation) is climbable material connecting corridor->R2 (rows 16-23). (3) R2's visible B/A/8/8/7/7 cluster is a SOCKET: stepping on it consumes it and reveals a 2x2 QUAD of buttons (8/B/A/7) at panel rows 46-49. Each quad click ADVANCES the lower-middle checker's color-type cycle 6/7 -> D/8 -> C/B -> 9/A -> 6/7 (any button = +1; covered clicks work silently). (4) TELEPORT NETWORK: stand on the checker + click big-6 teleports to the same-type twin: 6/7 pairs with the lower-right checker, C/B with the top-left room R1 checker, 9/A with the checker at the centre of the panel-diagram look-alike box at rows 56-61 cols 32-37 (the 'launcher'); D/8 has NO twin -> 6-click then rotates but does not teleport. (5) THE LAUNCHER: its four dithered 1/0 exit cells are walkable; standing on one LIGHTS the matching F/C/E/A D-pad button (F=up,C=left,E=right,A=down), and a lit button moves THE BIG 8-RING 4 cells that way. The ring floats over wall/void and restores cells on departure (no carving). (6) LATCH-MERGE: driving the big ring concentric with the C-structure's embedded small 8-ring and clicking the wide 8-bar (revealed by the earlier 8-socket, rows 17-19) MERGES them into a latched C+8 assembly; the D-pad then drags the ENTIRE C structure (still 6-rotatable). (7) MOVEMENT RULE: assembly cells may overlap wall only at rows >= 26; in rows <= 25 (the upper room band) only void-overlap is allowed, and '2' room cells are NEVER enterable - so the dog-legged void channel (cols 20-23 rows 8-19, box rows 20-23 cols 20-31, strip cols 28-31 rows 24-27) cannot be traversed by the 20-cell-long assembly, and (8) RAW VOID IS NOT AVATAR-WALKABLE (tested from a tower-top). Net: no discovered mechanism reaches the goal room (rows 4-11 cols 32-49, B block at 6-7,46-47).",
 "narrative": "Replayed the banked 322-action prefix from fresh reset; frame_level==5 confirmed (level 6 puzzle). Probed panel controls: big-6 toggles C rotation H/V, flips every checker phase, and teleports if the avatar stands on a checker; big-B cycles the shelves; the F/C/E/A D-pad and the revealed 8-bar were condition-gated no-ops everywhere at first. Walked onto the color-8 socket (right room) which dissolved it and revealed the 8-bar (rows 17-19). Dead ends: 8-bar/D-pad/ACTION5/object-clicks in both C rotations, on/off checkers. Breakthrough 1: descended out of the lower-middle room onto shelf-A when a B-phase placed it under cols 18-19, learned the 6-phase shelf machine and its avatar-support refusal rule, rode it west to the corridor, rotated C vertical and climbed the C column into R2. Breakthrough 2: stepped on R2's B/A/8877 cluster -> quad buttons revealed -> checker retype cycle understood -> teleport network mapped (LR, R1, launcher). Breakthrough 3: from the launcher's dither exits drove the big 8-ring, discovered concentric latch via the 8-bar, and dragged/rotated the whole C+8 assembly. Tried to park it as a horizontal bridge at rows 8-11 spanning cols 12-31 (R1 -> goal room walkway): blocked by the rows<=25 wall-overlap ban. V-tower up the void strip: blocked by the channel dog-leg (strip cols jump 20-23 -> 28-31 between row bands). Swept R1 (empty) and LR fully - no further reveals. Tested the R2-hint combos (9/A+big-B etc.) - the hint turned out to just preview the quad layout. Final probes: assembly cannot enter '2' rooms (refused adjacent to LM), but IS boardable from inside LM when parked with its column at cols 28-29 (climbed it to rows 28-29); stepping from the tower top into raw void refused -> void not walkable. Ended at 614 env steps with the avatar mid-tower; no level-6 win. Remaining unknown: the purpose of the D/8 checker type (no twin found - suspect a D/8 twin must be created somewhere, possibly the intended goal-room entry) and the row-63 tick counter (reached ~24/64; some refused actions tick).",
